  "text": "**Assessing the three proposals**\n\n- **Solution 1 (ratio 1)** is unlikely. It assumes the $\\alpha$-eigenspace of $U_\\wp$ stays one-dimensional as the level grows. Finite-slope multiplicities in level $\\Gamma_1(\\wp^r)$ generally grow with $r$, as in the classical Gouvêa–Mazur setting, so the inclusion $S_k(\\Gamma_1(\\mathfrak n\\wp))\\subset S_k(\\Gamma_1(\\mathfrak n\\wp^r))$ alone does not give equal multiplicities.\n- **Solution 2 (ratio $r$)** matches the expected behaviour. The multiplicity of a finite-slope eigensystem should grow linearly in the $\\wp$-power level. I recall this as the main theorem of Hattori's work on Drinfeld cuspforms of higher level, though I could not verify the exact statement here.\n- **Solution 3 (ratio $q^{2D(r-1)}$)** is not supported by its own reasoning. It hedges between several candidate exponents, and the index-counting argument it sketches does not determine a multiplicity ratio. The answer appears to be a guess.\n\nI'm going with Solution 2. The main uncertainty is that I'm relying on recall of the literature rather than a checked derivation.\n\nCHOICE: 2",
